sycl: decode NVFP4 scales and codes without pow() or table lookups

HomeBrain patch on ggml-sycl. Applies on top of 0008.
Upstream tracking: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/32757

Inkling's routed experts are NVFP4. The MoE mat-vec built each UE4M3
sub-block scale with sycl::pow() and decoded the E2M1 codes through
get_int_from_table_16, whose byte permutes are emulated with 64-bit shifts.
At decode it took 4x the MXFP4 time for the same bytes, about half of each
token. ggml_sycl_ue4m3_to_fp32 now builds the float from bits (bit-identical
to the CPU ldexpf reference), the dot product uses the SWAR
get_int_from_mxfp4, and the grouped GEMM's private pow-free copy goes away.
The grouped GEMM's NVFP4 stage decodes four codes at a time with the same
SWAR helper instead of one kvalues_mxfp4 load per value.

B60, test-backend-ops perf, 128 experts, top-8, Inkling shapes:
  gate_up [2304 x 2304], 1 token:     300.9 -> 82.3 us
  down    [1152 -> 2304], 1 token:    182.9 -> 50.3 us
  gate_up, 512 tokens:               7193 -> 5534 us
  down,    512 tokens:               3637 -> 2942 us

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
index d47101187..8e7cfc55f 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-sycl/common.hpp
@@ -1194,15 +1194,14 @@ static __dpct_inline__ float ggml_sycl_ue4m3_to_fp32(uint8_t x) {
     if (x == 0 || x == 0x7F) {
         return 0.0f;
     }
-    const int exp = (x >> 3) & 0xF;
-    const int man = x & 0x7;
-    float raw;
+    // the * 0.5f halves the doubled e2m1 values of kvalues_mxfp4. Built from bits: pow() here was most
+    // of the NVFP4 GEMV's cost. A normal scale is the float with exponent exp - 7 - 1, mantissa on top.
+    const uint32_t exp = (x >> 3) & 0xF;
+    const uint32_t man = x & 0x7;
     if (exp == 0) {
-        raw = man * (1.0f / 8.0f) * sycl::pow(2.0f, -6.0f);
-    } else {
-        raw = (1.0f + man / 8.0f) * sycl::pow(2.0f, (float) exp - 7.0f);
+        return (float) man * (1.0f / 1024.0f);
     }
-    return raw * 0.5f;
+    return sycl::bit_cast<float>(((exp + 119u) << 23) | (man << 20));
 }
 
 #endif // GGML_SYCL_COMMON_HPP
